# IMPROVEMENT_PLAN.md Phase 5. Moderate check set: bugprone/performance
# checks are high-value and low-noise; modernize/readability are limited
# to a few uncontroversial ones rather than enabled wholesale, since a
# Qt-heavy codebase (QObject parent-ownership, signal/slot connections,
# QString-heavy string handling) trips a lot of generic C++
# cppcoreguidelines-style checks that don't apply cleanly to Qt idioms.
#
# NOT yet run against this codebase (no clang-tidy binary available in the
# environment this was authored in -- see IMPROVEMENT_PLAN.md Phase 5).
# The CI lint workflow's first real run is expected to surface findings
# that haven't been triaged yet; until then, treat this job as
# informational (see .github/workflows/lint.yml's continue-on-error) rather
# than a hard gate, so it doesn't turn PRs red for pre-existing findings no
# one has looked at.
Checks: >
  -*,
  bugprone-*,
  -bugprone-easily-swappable-parameters,
  performance-*,
  modernize-use-nullptr,
  modernize-use-override,
  modernize-use-default-member-init,
  readability-braces-around-statements,
  readability-redundant-string-cstr,
  readability-simplify-boolean-expr
WarningsAsErrors: ''
HeaderFilterRegex: 'engine/src/.*'
FormatStyle: none
